{
  "analysis": "The minimal test compiled and produced a 32-bit little-endian MIPS ELF with `main`, but the VM failed at a glibc function using SPECIAL3 function 0x3b (RDHWR), a MIPS32r2 instruction not supported by the VM. The compiler defaults to MIPS32r2 and glibc static libraries use unsupported instructions. I need to either compile for an older architecture and/or avoid glibc dependencies, or implement direct syscalls in the source.",
  "plan": "First test whether `-march=mips1` reduces unsupported instructions. If glibc still uses RDHWR, I will need to avoid glibc or provide custom syscall wrappers. I will also inspect the VM's supported instruction set more carefully to understand constraints.",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "mipsel-linux-gnu-gcc-12 -static -march=mips1 -mno-mips16 -mno-interlink-mips16 -O0 -fno-asynchronous-unwind-tables -fno-unwind-tables -ffunction-sections -fdata-sections -Wl,--gc-sections -o /tmp/hello_mips1 /tmp/hello_mips.c\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "mipsel-linux-gnu-readelf -h /tmp/hello_mips1 | grep -E 'Class|Data|Machine|Flags|Entry'; mipsel-linux-gnu-objdump -d /tmp/hello_mips1 | grep -E 'rdhwr|0x3b' | head\n",
      "duration": 0.1
    },
    {
      "keystrokes": "cp /tmp/hello_mips1 /app/doomgeneric_mips && node vm.js | head -20\n",
      "duration": 1.0
    }
  ]
}
